---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Methodology">
  <section style="padding:2.5rem 0 1rem; max-width:70ch;">
    <h1>Methodology</h1>

    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>This archive records media coverage of Jensen Huang: news reports, columns, opinion pieces, investigations, analyses, podcasts and satire. We record positive, neutral, mixed and critical coverage in the same way.</p>

    <h2>What we record per article</h2>
    <p>Headline, publication, byline(s), publication date, article type, main topic, evidence level, and a sentiment label describing the article's framing. Every entry links to the original source.</p>

    <h2>What sentiment means — and doesn't</h2>
    <p>Sentiment is a description of an article's framing, not a judgement of its accuracy. A critical article may be correct; a supportive article may be wrong. Readers should follow the source link and evaluate the evidence themselves.</p>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not infer motivation, ethnicity, politics or personal conflict from a journalist's name, affiliation or stance.</li>
      <li>We do not treat shared topics, similar framings, close timing or common funding as proof of coordination. These are observations, not conclusions.</li>
      <li>We do not reproduce full copyrighted articles. Summaries are short and link back to the source.</li>
      <li>We do not publish private information about journalists. Profile pages show published bylines in this archive and nothing else.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Verification</h2>
    <p>Metadata verification (headline, URL, date, byline, publication) is separate from claim verification. "Verified" on a row means we opened the source page and confirmed the metadata. It does not mean the article's claims are correct.</p>

    <h2>Funding transparency</h2>
    <p>Funding relationships are recorded only when supported by a verifiable public disclosure. A funding relationship is a factual link between a funder and a recipient; it is not evidence of editorial influence over any specific article. We do not auto-link funders to individual stories unless the funder itself disclosed support for that specific story. See <a href="/funding">Funding</a>.</p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>If you find an error in our metadata, classification or source link, open an issue or email the maintainer. We log every correction, keeping both the original entry and the revised entry visible. See <a href="/corrections">Corrections</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
